# Commit Recommendation

Whenever repository files were changed, append **exactly one** recommended Conventional Commit as the **final section** of the response (after the Azerbaijani summary).

**Format:**

```text
Recommended commit:
`type: concise description`
```

**Rules:**

- Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, etc.).
- Prefer a single commit. If multiple commits are genuinely needed, explain why and recommend each one.
- Never recommend a commit when no repository files changed.
- Never claim a commit was created unless it was actually created.
- Do not create a git commit unless the user explicitly asks.
